  {
   "id": "why1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 500,
   "y": 140,
   "width": 357,
   "height": 18,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100026,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700182,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why code is the PK, not a surrogate id",
   "originalText": "Why code is the PK, not a surrogate id",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "why1b",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 500,
   "y": 166,
   "width": 471,
   "height": 97,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100027,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700189,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "On a clustered engine the row data lives in the leaf of\nthe code index - so GET /{code} is ONE descent and you\nhave the whole row. With a surrogate id it is two:\ndescend code -> find id -> descend the primary index.\nAt 5,800 reads/sec that is 5,800 avoidable descents a\nsecond, forever, to gain a key nothing in the design uses.",
   "originalText": "On a clustered engine the row data lives in the leaf of\nthe code index - so GET /{code} is ONE descent and you\nhave the whole row. With a surrogate id it is two:\ndescend code -> find id -> descend the primary index.\nAt 5,800 reads/sec that is 5,800 avoidable descents a\nsecond, forever, to gain a key nothing in the design uses.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "why2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 500,
   "y": 306,
   "width": 403,
   "height": 18,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100028,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700196,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why long_url_hash is indexed but NOT unique",
   "originalText": "Why long_url_hash is indexed but NOT unique",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "why2b",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 500,
   "y": 332,
   "width": 415,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100029,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700203,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Unique here would enforce deduplication - the exact\nproduct behaviour the design rejected, because it\ncollapses expiry, deletion, ownership and analytics\nonto one row. It exists for abuse takedown instead.",
   "originalText": "Unique here would enforce deduplication - the exact\nproduct behaviour the design rejected, because it\ncollapses expiry, deletion, ownership and analytics\nonto one row. It exists for abuse takedown instead.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "why3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 500,
   "y": 424,
   "width": 376,
   "height": 18,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100030,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700210,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why a hash rather than indexing long_url",
   "originalText": "Why a hash rather than indexing long_url",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "why3b",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 500,
   "y": 450,
   "width": 447,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100031,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700217,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "long_url averages 200 bytes with a long tail past 500 -\na wide, variable-length, poor index key. A fixed 8-byte\nhash is dense and uniform. Truncated-hash collisions\ndo happen, so queries re-verify long_url in the WHERE.",
   "originalText": "long_url averages 200 bytes with a long tail past 500 -\na wide, variable-length, poor index key. A fixed 8-byte\nhash is dense and uniform. Truncated-hash collisions\ndo happen, so queries re-verify long_url in the WHERE.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1080,
   "y": 108,
   "width": 457,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
